    "description": "**Whether you’re an experienced professional or just getting started, your contributions matter at Fortra. If you’re passionate about tackling meaningful challenges alongside talented team members committed to helping each other succeed, all while having lots of fun, we want to hear from you. We offer competitive benefits and salaries, personal and professional development opportunities, flexibility, and much more!**\n\nFortra’s Offensive Security portfolio brings together industry-leading adversary simulation technology, offensive security expertise, and hands-on training. Following the addition of Zero-Point Security to Fortra, we are expanding our training capabilities to help offensive security professionals develop practical, real-world skills across red teaming, adversary simulation, and penetration testing.  \n  \nWe are looking for an Offensive Security Training Content Developer to help build and evolve Fortra’s offensive security training portfolio. This is a hands-on technical role combining offensive security expertise, technical education, lab development, and content creation.  \n  \nYou will be responsible for maintaining and improving the Zero-Point Security Red Team Operations courses, supporting and expanding Cobalt Strike training and certification content, and developing new courses around emerging offensive security techniques and Fortra technologies.  \n  \nYou should enjoy understanding offensive tradecraft in depth, explaining complex concepts clearly, and turning technical knowledge into practical exercises that allow students to learn by doing.\n\n**WHAT YOU’LL DO**\n\n  \n\n- Maintain and continuously improve Red Team Operations, Cobalt Strike, and related offensive security training content, ensuring it reflects current tradecraft, product capabilities, and recommended operator practices.\n- Design and develop new courses, modules, hands-on exercises, assessments, certifications, and learning paths for Fortra’s offensive security training portfolio.\n- Research modern adversary tactics, techniques, and procedures, translating them into safe, realistic, and authorized training scenarios.\n- Create, document, test, and maintain practical lab environments - including supporting infrastructure, scripts, configurations, and resources - to ensure exercises are accurate, reproducible, reliable, and achieve their intended learning outcomes.\n- Write clear, structured technical learning materials, including lessons, walkthroughs, lab guides, reference documentation, quizzes, and exercises for audiences with varied experience levels.\n- Collaborate with Zero-Point Security experts, Cobalt Strike engineers and researchers, product teams, and other stakeholders to turn research, tooling, and product capabilities into effective training.\n- Gather and incorporate feedback from students, instructors, customers, support teams, and internal stakeholders to improve course quality and the overall learning experience.\n- Help shape the training roadmap by identifying skills gaps, emerging techniques, new technologies, and opportunities for new courses or certifications.\n- Establish consistent standards for technical accuracy, instructional quality, lab design, terminology, and course structure across the training portfolio.\n- Produce supporting educational content - such as demonstrations, videos, webinars, workshops, blog posts, and presentations - when appropriate.\n- Ensure all training involving offensive security capabilities is designed and presented responsibly for legitimate, authorized security testing and education.\n\n \n\n**QUALIFICATIONS**\n\n  \n\n- Strong hands-on experience in offensive security, including red teaming, penetration testing, adversary simulation, security research, or related discipline.\n- Strong understanding of modern red-team operations and adversary-simulation lifecycle, including common techniques across initial access, command and control, privilege escalation, credential access, lateral movement, persistence, and post-exploitation.\n- Practical experience with Cobalt Strike or comparable command-and-control and adversarysimulation platforms; advanced Cobalt Strike tradecraft or extensibility experience is a plus.\n- Strong working knowledge of Windows environments, Active Directory, and, ideally, Windows internals, endpoint controls, EDR, detection engineering, or defensive telemetry.\n- Ability to build, troubleshoot, automate, and maintain realistic cybersecurity lab environments, including multi-host Active Directory environments; familiarity with virtualization, cloud infrastructure, containers, infrastructure-as-code, or automated provisioning is desirable.\n- Experience with scripting or programming languages used in offensive security, such as PowerShell, Python, C#, or C, and comfort evaluating technical documentation, proof ofconcept code, security research, and offensive tooling.\n- Ability to independently research a subject, validate it in a lab, and turn findings into repeatable, high-quality training content.\n- Excellent technical writing, verbal communication, and instructional design skills, with the ability to explain complex concepts clearly to audiences at different experience levels.\n- Strong attention to detail when validating exercises, commands, code examples, instructions, and lab environments, along with experience managing technical content through structured documentation and version-control workflows.\n- Experience developing or delivering cybersecurity education, such as courses, certifications, labs, CTFs, workshops, mentoring, conference presentations, or online training.\n- Familiarity with learning management systems, assessment design, technical video production, or public-facing technical content is beneficial.\n- Experience with other Fortra Offensive Security technologies, including Outflank Security Tooling or Core Impact, is a plus.\n- Ability to work independently and collaboratively with researchers, engineers, product teams, and subject matter experts.\n- High ethical standards, sound judgment, and a demonstrated commitment to responsible use of offensive security techniques.\n- Active interest in offensive security research and continuous learning; experience using AI-assisted workflows for research, content development, labs, or quality assurance is beneficial.\n\n \n\nPREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n- Completion of Red Team Operations I / CRTO, Red Team Operations II / Red Team Lead, Cobalt Strike training, or comparable advanced offensive security training.\n\n  \n\n**Compensation**: 115,000.00 USD - 140,000.00 USD\n\nAt Fortra, we’re breaking the attack chain. Ready to join us?\n\nAt Fortra, our compensation philosophy prioritizes fair market value and internal equity, aligning with your experience and specialized skill set.\n\nAs a full-time, exempt employee at Fortra, you’ll enjoy a comprehensive benefits package that includes:\n\n- Health, dental, and vision coverage as of hire\n- Immediate enrollment in 401(k), HSA, and FSA plans\n- Flexible PTO policy\n- Tuition and personal enrichment reimbursement\n- Option to enroll in ID Theft Protection Program\n\n*At Fortra, work is only part of the story. Explore what Life at Fortra is all about, from perks that support holistic wellbeing to a culture that keeps you connected and empowered to make an impact beyond the job.*\n\nVisit our website to learn more about why employees choose to work for Fortra. Remember to connect with us on LinkedIn.  \n  \nAs an EEO/Affirmative Action Employer, all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran or disability status.",
